    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-2288",
      "problem": "The tape diagram below shows the ratio between small and big tokens in a desk game. What is the ratio of big tokens to all tokens?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14187307/assets/5b779b66fb6e6717e102398153f09f3cb70582a4333a68ad2aeeb97fced47c9b.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The tape diagram for big tokens shows $4$ boxes. So, there are $4$ big tokens.\n\nAltogether, there are $12+4=16$ boxes. So, there are $16$ tokens in all.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of big tokens to all tokens is $4:16.$",
